# Line-ending policy for content-addressed files.
#
# The v3.2 specification pack is checksummed: docs/v3.2/manifest.json records the
# SHA-256 of every file exactly as authored, and scripts/validate_v32_pack.py
# verifies them (requirement R22). A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites every text file to CRLF, which changes those bytes and made the pack
# look corrupt after a branch checkout.
#
# Pinning these paths to LF keeps the working tree byte-identical to the pack, so
# the manifest check verifies content rather than the checkout convention. The
# validator also normalises line endings before hashing, so this is defence in
# depth rather than the only thing holding the check up.
docs/v3.2/**        text eol=lf
litsearch/contracts/**  text eol=lf
fixtures/**         text eol=lf

# Binary and generated assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
web/dist/** -text
litsearch/web/static/** -text
